WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
We'll make a seven-second moving cover for Stillform,
an alpine photography journal.

00:00:03.375 --> 00:00:07.150
Choose Open project and open the Stillform starter folder.

00:00:07.208 --> 00:00:11.000
The starter has a blank scene, typefaces and reusable
cover components. Open Assets to add the photograph.

00:00:11.083 --> 00:00:14.750
Choose Import files, select grand-teton.jpg and open it.

00:00:14.792 --> 00:00:17.150
The photograph now appears alongside the project's typefaces.

00:00:17.208 --> 00:00:23.070 line:4%
With Codex selected, describe the first cut: one photograph,
a masthead over it and a title entrance at 0.08 seconds.

00:00:23.125 --> 00:00:25.650
Send the brief to Codex inside OMS.

00:00:25.708 --> 00:00:31.700
Codex assembles the scene using Photograph and Cover,
then checks its render. The processing wait is shortened.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:39.150
Play the first cut. Watch how quickly the title
appears over the landscape.

00:00:39.208 --> 00:00:42.650 line:4%
Pause at two seconds. Select Region
and drag a box around the masthead.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:47.990 line:4%
Add the note: “Let the photograph breathe.
Bring the title in half a second later.”

00:00:48.042 --> 00:00:53.280 line:4%
Send the marked frame to Codex and ask it
to leave the rest of the film as it is.

00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:59.400
Codex moves the entrance to 0.58 seconds and checks
the revised frames. The processing wait is shortened.

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:06.900
Replay the seven-second cut at normal speed.
The landscape now has a moment before the masthead enters.

00:01:06.958 --> 00:01:12.890
Both openings play together at normal speed, twice.
Watch the photograph on the right.

00:01:12.958 --> 00:01:16.030
Choose Export MP4. OMS checks the film
and shows the output dimensions and frame rate.

00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:19.860
Save Stillform.mp4 in the project folder.

00:01:19.917 --> 00:01:25.850
OMS renders the frames locally and confirms the file is ready.
The middle of the render wait is cut.

00:01:25.917 --> 00:01:28.000
The exported MP4, played at normal speed.
